WEBVTT

01:40.660 --> 01:41.500
I stood here,

01:42.180 --> 01:43.620
under this sky of burning sunset.

01:45.160 --> 01:46.920
For the first time, I prayed in my heart.

01:47.640 --> 01:49.180
Let the day in Hongyang

01:50.780 --> 01:52.900
be a cloudy day without sunset glows.

01:54.460 --> 01:56.240
Yingtao must not see the sunset glow.

01:57.040 --> 01:58.660
So she won't think of me.

01:58.700 --> 02:00.380
Let her be happy…

02:03.100 --> 02:04.080
even just a little.

02:06.100 --> 02:07.880
Maybe you were right.

02:08.419 --> 02:09.940
Maybe on that day,

02:09.979 --> 02:11.600
I didn't see any sunset.

02:12.760 --> 02:14.140
Most days,

02:15.320 --> 02:17.620
I was in the library

02:17.660 --> 02:19.020
or stuck in class at night.

02:19.680 --> 02:21.420
I didn't get to see sunsets anyway.

02:27.020 --> 02:28.920
I know that's just me lying to myself.

02:29.540 --> 02:31.600
It's not the sunset

02:31.640 --> 02:32.960
that reminds you of me.

02:33.560 --> 02:34.940
It's because you thought of me

02:36.980 --> 02:38.380
that led you to the view of sunsets.

02:39.580 --> 02:41.000
So, I can't blame your sadness

02:41.040 --> 02:42.680
on the sunset.

02:45.820 --> 02:47.260
It's me. I'm to be blame.

02:49.720 --> 02:51.740
There are times I can't stand myself.

02:51.780 --> 02:53.140
I don't even know why,

02:54.060 --> 02:55.720
but when I left you that night,

02:56.540 --> 02:57.760
I told you,

02:59.320 --> 03:00.600
"Don't forget me, Yingtao."

03:02.380 --> 03:03.380
But the truth is,

03:03.420 --> 03:06.040
the people I care about, near or far,

03:07.900 --> 03:09.720
I never had the strength
to hold on to any of them.

03:10.980 --> 03:13.100
There were days my chest felt so tight,

03:13.140 --> 03:14.840
I thought I'd explode.

03:15.840 --> 03:16.880
For the first time,

03:17.420 --> 03:19.340
I wanted to find a place
and cry my heart out.

03:20.720 --> 03:21.880
I ducked behind a pillar,

03:22.520 --> 03:23.840
but tourists were taking photos.

03:24.380 --> 03:25.560
I went down the stairs,

03:28.320 --> 03:29.620
and there were couples kissing.

03:32.300 --> 03:34.420
So, I held it in.

03:34.460 --> 03:36.300
I held it in all the way until around

03:36.340 --> 03:37.240
ten o'clock at night.

03:38.120 --> 03:39.040
The crowd thinned out.

03:39.880 --> 03:41.360
I bought a Ferris wheel ticket.

03:47.780 --> 03:49.200
I sat alone in a cabin

03:49.920 --> 03:51.760
and finally let it all out.

03:53.180 --> 03:54.320
That was September 6th,

03:54.960 --> 03:55.980
of 2008.

03:57.940 --> 04:00.460
That night,
Jiang Qiaoxi was a miserable guy.

04:02.880 --> 04:03.880
Because he had no idea

04:05.020 --> 04:07.100
that 639 days later,

04:07.660 --> 04:08.800
he'd be standing here again.

04:10.680 --> 04:12.320
Lin Yingtao would be right beside him.

04:40.040 --> 04:41.620
Jiang Qiaoxi, you dummy.

04:43.300 --> 04:45.160
Why don't you just call Lin Yingtao?

04:46.980 --> 04:48.000
Tell her

04:48.600 --> 04:49.720
you feel terrible.

04:49.760 --> 04:51.720
She would've fought through it with you.

04:52.420 --> 04:54.860
But even if you don't, it doesn't matter.

04:55.600 --> 04:58.380
Because in 639 days,

04:58.420 --> 04:59.760
Lin Yingtao

05:00.680 --> 05:02.040
will come looking for you.

05:03.140 --> 05:04.460
No matter where you are,

05:05.740 --> 05:07.460
I'll always find you.

05:09.040 --> 05:10.380
Don't sell yourself short.

05:11.300 --> 05:13.140
You've done something amazing.

05:14.500 --> 05:15.880
And from this day on,

05:18.480 --> 05:19.660
I'm staying right by your side.

05:21.880 --> 05:22.840
You're stuck with me now.

05:24.820 --> 05:25.680
No more running.

05:34.300 --> 05:36.280
If only I'd been there back then.

05:36.880 --> 05:37.940
You could've stepped

05:37.980 --> 05:39.280
off that Ferris wheel

05:40.380 --> 05:41.300
and fallen into my arms.

05:43.660 --> 05:45.020
You weren't late.

05:45.960 --> 05:46.940
It is me

05:47.800 --> 05:49.080
who couldn't find my way home.

05:55.700 --> 05:56.540
Jiang Qiaoxi,

05:57.500 --> 05:59.120
where can we watch the sunrise
in Hong Kong?

05:59.680 --> 06:00.740
Let's go find it.

06:08.220 --> 06:09.220
It's beautiful.

06:12.940 --> 06:13.780
Let's keep walking.

06:14.420 --> 06:15.260
There.

07:22.880 --> 07:23.800
Jiang Qiaoxi.

07:25.620 --> 07:26.480
Back at the pier,

07:26.520 --> 07:27.520
you told me

07:29.200 --> 07:30.960
how much you hated yourself

07:31.000 --> 07:33.100
for asking me not to forget you.

07:36.340 --> 07:37.680
Please don't think that way.

07:39.460 --> 07:40.540
All these years,

07:40.580 --> 07:42.100
even without hearing from you,

07:42.140 --> 07:43.460
those words

07:44.860 --> 07:47.020
reminded me you still needed me.

07:51.000 --> 07:52.760
That's why I kept going.

07:53.760 --> 07:55.100
So no, you didn't do anything wrong.

08:00.800 --> 08:01.640
Yingtao,

08:03.360 --> 08:04.760
have you ever heard

08:04.800 --> 08:06.540
the story of Wei Sheng and the bridge?

08:08.480 --> 08:10.020
There once was a man

08:10.620 --> 08:11.660
named Wei Sheng.

08:12.200 --> 08:13.800
He fell in love with a woman.

08:15.860 --> 08:18.040
But her parents were against it.

08:18.080 --> 08:19.600
So, they made a pact

08:19.640 --> 08:20.760
to run away together.

08:21.940 --> 08:23.640
They agreed to meet at dusk

08:24.500 --> 08:26.500
by the bridge on the outskirts of town.

08:27.540 --> 08:28.800
But when the day came,

08:29.460 --> 08:31.840
he waited, but the lady didn't show up.

08:31.880 --> 08:32.860
Not long after,

08:33.720 --> 08:34.880
a flash flood hit.

08:35.780 --> 08:37.120
Wei Sheng was in danger.

08:40.000 --> 08:41.340
But he refused to break

08:41.380 --> 08:42.539
the promise between them.

08:44.980 --> 08:46.500
He clung to that bridge pillar

08:48.520 --> 08:51.160
until the woman arrived
and found him drowned.

08:53.360 --> 08:54.460
He never let go.

09:03.960 --> 09:06.000
Well, I'm not Wei Sheng.

09:06.040 --> 09:07.940
If the one doesn't show up,

09:07.980 --> 09:08.960
I'll go find them.

09:09.700 --> 09:11.100
If they run,

09:11.940 --> 09:12.780
I'll go seek.

09:14.080 --> 09:16.000
If I can't catch up,
I'll block their path.

09:16.540 --> 09:17.960
Either way, you're not getting away.

09:19.200 --> 09:21.420
If I see even the tiniest sign
that you still love me,

09:23.240 --> 09:24.200
I'll act on it.

09:26.760 --> 09:27.960
You're not getting away.

09:41.360 --> 09:42.560
Your hair,

09:43.760 --> 09:45.100
your eyebrows…

09:47.860 --> 09:49.040
your eyes,

09:50.780 --> 09:51.820
your nose…

09:54.040 --> 09:55.020
your mouth…

09:59.280 --> 10:00.300
Every part of you

10:01.560 --> 10:02.560
is mine.

11:06.180 --> 11:07.180
You're awake.

11:26.080 --> 11:27.100
You know

11:29.080 --> 11:30.920
why I wanted to see the sunrise?

11:33.160 --> 11:34.360
Three years ago,

11:36.580 --> 11:38.640
when you all bid your goodbyes
to me in Qunshan,

11:39.200 --> 11:40.040
you said,

11:42.480 --> 11:43.940
"Sunsets are not going away.

11:44.840 --> 11:46.460
They're just

11:46.500 --> 11:47.720
on their way back.

11:49.020 --> 11:50.940
Next time we see them,

11:50.980 --> 11:52.900
they'll be the rosy light of dawn."

11:53.720 --> 11:54.940
Welcome home,

11:56.220 --> 11:57.060
Jiang Qiaoxi.

11:58.640 --> 11:59.480
I'm back.

12:01.380 --> 12:02.420
And I'm not leaving again.

12:06.280 --> 12:07.440
Go on.

12:07.480 --> 12:08.440
Say that again.

12:09.380 --> 12:10.300
I want to record it.

12:10.340 --> 12:12.100
Let the sunrise be our witness.

12:12.140 --> 12:13.440
I'm back.

12:13.480 --> 12:15.080
And I'm not leaving again.

12:15.900 --> 12:17.060
I, Jiang Qiaoxi, swear,

12:17.960 --> 12:18.840
nothing in this world

12:18.880 --> 12:19.980
can keep me

12:20.020 --> 12:21.840
from staying by Lin Yingtao's side.

12:23.500 --> 12:24.900
Not a financial crisis.

12:25.540 --> 12:27.140
Not a volcanic eruption.

12:27.780 --> 12:28.880
Not a tsunami.

12:28.920 --> 12:30.860
Not a heavy suitcase.

12:31.780 --> 12:34.480
Not a water-stained wall.

12:34.520 --> 12:35.580
Not a broken AC unit.

12:35.620 --> 12:36.820
Not overcast skies.

12:36.860 --> 12:37.700
Not pride.

12:37.740 --> 12:38.800
Not shame.

12:38.840 --> 12:39.680
Not ego.

12:39.720 --> 12:40.780
Not fallen leaves.

12:40.820 --> 12:42.940
Not a rusted fence.

12:42.980 --> 12:43.880
Not even

12:44.560 --> 12:45.840
morning dew.

12:45.880 --> 12:48.060
Not moss-covered stone paths.

12:48.100 --> 12:49.160
Not an anthill.

12:49.900 --> 12:51.020
Not even

12:51.600 --> 12:52.980
a plastic bottle

12:53.020 --> 12:54.220
that missed the trash can.

12:54.260 --> 12:55.120
Missed bottles?

13:08.780 --> 13:09.620
Jiang Qiaoxi.

13:12.120 --> 13:13.360
Maybe I shouldn't have

13:13.400 --> 13:15.140
brought you to see the sunset.

13:16.380 --> 13:17.960
Sunsets are beautiful,

13:18.580 --> 13:19.840
but they fade too fast.

13:20.940 --> 13:22.580
I should've taken you to see the sunrise.

13:25.500 --> 13:26.880
Though, in that case,

13:26.920 --> 13:28.600
you wouldn't be Jiang Qiaoxi.

13:28.640 --> 13:29.920
You should be at the east of the crest,
as Jiang Qiaodong.

14:21.820 --> 14:22.720
Hey, cousin-in-law.

14:22.760 --> 14:25.060
Vincent, your cousin's missing.

14:31.900 --> 14:33.200
Have you seen my cousin's wife?

14:35.220 --> 14:36.180
Qiaoxi.

14:36.220 --> 14:37.220
- Cousin-in-law.
- You're here.

14:37.260 --> 14:38.400
Your cousin can barely stand.

14:38.440 --> 14:40.360
I'm scared he might do something stupid.

14:43.460 --> 14:45.160
Don't worry. I'll go find him right now.

14:50.860 --> 14:51.740
Come on.

15:03.340 --> 15:04.800
Where do you think he'd go?

15:19.760 --> 15:20.840
Jiang Qiaoxi.

15:22.820 --> 15:23.720
Look.

15:26.660 --> 15:27.500
Cousin!

15:28.700 --> 15:29.820
Cousin!

15:31.180 --> 15:32.480
Is that him?

15:32.520 --> 15:33.540
Jiang Ruocheng!

15:40.380 --> 15:41.380
Cousin!

15:43.820 --> 15:45.260
Jeez.

15:45.300 --> 15:47.320
We just snuck off for ice cream.

15:47.860 --> 15:49.600
No need to send a whole rescue squad.

15:50.800 --> 15:51.920
Not him?

15:52.840 --> 15:53.720
Come on.

16:41.700 --> 16:43.020
Mercy Hospital at Victoria Harbor.

16:43.060 --> 16:44.180
We have a missing patient.

16:45.340 --> 16:46.460
Male, 37 years old.

16:47.100 --> 16:48.180
About five foot ten.

16:48.220 --> 16:49.140
In a hospital gown.

16:52.460 --> 16:53.440
It happened

16:53.480 --> 16:54.640
about an hour ago.

16:55.980 --> 16:57.000
Yes, I'm his family.

16:57.500 --> 16:58.480
Ruocheng is home?

16:59.980 --> 17:01.160
Thanks for your help.

17:01.840 --> 17:03.040
He didn't even have money on him.

17:03.740 --> 17:05.400
Your cousin went home.

17:08.900 --> 17:09.839
Hey, I'm sorry.

17:09.880 --> 17:11.220
I think we found him.

17:11.260 --> 17:12.160
Sorry for the trouble.

17:12.200 --> 17:14.859
Could you ask him
if he knows how worried we were?

17:15.800 --> 17:17.460
You went off on your own,

17:17.500 --> 17:20.520
and now you're back safe.

17:20.560 --> 17:21.680
Jiang Ruocheng!

17:33.380 --> 17:34.500
How'd you even find this place?

17:35.360 --> 17:37.860
I've been in the hospital for so long,

17:37.900 --> 17:41.600
most of that time stuck in bed,

17:42.680 --> 17:44.580
couldn't even get up.

17:45.120 --> 17:47.500
All I could do was lie there,
staring at the ceiling.

17:47.540 --> 17:48.580
Sometimes I'd wonder,

17:48.620 --> 17:49.940
without me around, how did you all

17:49.980 --> 17:51.180
get by these past few years?

17:53.180 --> 17:54.320
What I didn't expect

17:54.820 --> 17:56.800
was that this is how you've been living.

17:58.440 --> 17:59.520
No matter how we've lived,

18:00.160 --> 18:01.780
we still managed.

18:01.820 --> 18:03.000
You call this managing?

18:04.720 --> 18:06.260
If I'd known it'd turn out like this,

18:06.980 --> 18:07.820
that day…

18:08.620 --> 18:11.120
I'd rather you hadn't saved me.
You should've just let me die.

18:11.160 --> 18:13.800
What are you talking about?
Don't say things like that.

18:14.340 --> 18:15.300
You have no idea

18:15.340 --> 18:18.060
how much Yalin's been through
these past two years.

18:18.100 --> 18:20.880
You don't know how she got through it.

18:20.920 --> 18:22.640
You are getting better now,

18:22.680 --> 18:24.280
and you're here talking like this?

18:24.320 --> 18:26.300
Mom, it's because I know
how hard it's been for her.

18:26.960 --> 18:29.000
Look at me. Look at what I've become.

18:29.800 --> 18:31.240
I've lost everything.

18:31.780 --> 18:33.720
The place at Repulse Bay is gone.

18:33.760 --> 18:34.760
The money for Qiaoxi

18:34.800 --> 18:35.860
to study abroad is gone too.

18:35.900 --> 18:36.960
We're broke.

18:37.000 --> 18:37.980
We have nothing left.

18:38.520 --> 18:39.480
And all because

18:40.160 --> 18:41.220
you chose to save me.

18:41.260 --> 18:42.740
Now look where you're living.

18:42.780 --> 18:44.460
It's my fault you ended up like this.

18:44.500 --> 18:46.100
Don't you see that, Mom?

18:46.940 --> 18:48.380
Don't say anything more.

18:48.420 --> 18:49.260
Ruocheng,

18:51.020 --> 18:52.160
you didn't drag me down.

18:53.480 --> 18:54.560
I believed in you.

18:54.600 --> 18:56.380
If the doctors hadn't told me

18:56.940 --> 18:58.280
you might get better,

18:58.320 --> 18:59.820
I wouldn't have made it this far.

19:01.920 --> 19:03.500
You've always had something in you.

19:03.540 --> 19:05.560
This place is not
so different from before.

19:07.760 --> 19:09.600
There's nothing left in me.

19:09.640 --> 19:12.180
What's left for you to believe in?

19:13.320 --> 19:15.100
I've lost everything.

19:15.640 --> 19:16.820
Even holding my own daughter

19:17.540 --> 19:19.060
feels like a memory I can't reach anymore.

19:19.100 --> 19:20.720
Look at my legs.

19:20.760 --> 19:23.020
- I came home, saw my dad like that,
- It's fine…

19:23.060 --> 19:25.520
- and I couldn't even walk over to him.
- We will be fine…

19:25.560 --> 19:27.160
I've lost everything.

19:27.200 --> 19:28.980
Look at what I've become.

19:29.020 --> 19:31.760
- I'm just a wreck now.
- Jiang Ruocheng!

19:32.940 --> 19:33.880
I waited all this time,

19:33.920 --> 19:35.300
took care of you for so long.

19:35.820 --> 19:37.360
When you are finally getting better,

19:37.400 --> 19:39.440
I don't what to hear
something this cruel now.

19:40.660 --> 19:41.580
If that's all you've got,

19:41.620 --> 19:43.600
then maybe I'd rather
you stayed in the hospital.

19:43.640 --> 19:44.860
At least there was still hope.

19:45.820 --> 19:47.340
Right now,

19:47.380 --> 19:48.800
there's none.

19:49.380 --> 19:51.560
So, stop doing this to me.

19:51.600 --> 19:52.880
I'm so sorry.

19:52.920 --> 19:54.300
I'm so sorry, honey.

19:54.340 --> 19:55.560
I didn't know…

19:55.600 --> 19:56.500
Come on. Let's go.

19:56.540 --> 19:59.940
I'm a bad husband.

20:04.160 --> 20:05.600
I didn't know…

20:10.680 --> 20:11.560
It'll be alright.

20:43.480 --> 20:44.320
Excuse me.

20:44.360 --> 20:45.200
Are you ready to order?

20:45.240 --> 20:46.660
Two beers, please.

20:46.700 --> 20:47.900
Coming right up.

20:50.180 --> 20:52.380
I don't usually like you drinking.

20:53.120 --> 20:54.780
But I think today,

20:55.300 --> 20:56.240
we deserve a drink.

20:57.600 --> 20:59.600
Here you go. Two beers.

21:00.820 --> 21:01.860
Thanks.

21:01.900 --> 21:02.740
Thanks.

21:04.080 --> 21:04.980
Enjoy.

21:22.700 --> 21:25.260
That was my first time
meeting your cousin.

21:25.800 --> 21:27.720
Honestly? He was pretty much the same

21:27.760 --> 21:28.600
as how I pictured him.

21:29.340 --> 21:30.680
Carried himself with class.

21:30.720 --> 21:31.800
Good-looking too.

21:32.480 --> 21:34.120
If you look half that good

21:34.160 --> 21:35.900
when you're his age, I'll be happy.

21:37.320 --> 21:38.740
You didn't see him before.

21:39.420 --> 21:40.260
Back then,

21:40.300 --> 21:41.780
just one look in his eyes

21:42.460 --> 21:43.580
and you'd think

21:43.620 --> 21:45.800
there's nothing in the world
he couldn't do.

21:47.280 --> 21:49.360
He could kill it in business,

21:49.400 --> 21:51.540
take great care of his family,

21:52.440 --> 21:53.400
and still

21:54.500 --> 21:56.200
find time to pave the way

21:56.240 --> 21:57.980
for a clueless little cousin like me.

22:00.660 --> 22:02.800
I know you've always looked up to him.

22:04.160 --> 22:05.960
You puked on that jacket
he gave you as a kid

22:06.000 --> 22:07.420
and still kept it.

22:07.460 --> 22:09.100
I wanted to be like him.

22:10.300 --> 22:11.340
Responsible.

22:11.380 --> 22:12.560
Reliable.

22:12.600 --> 22:13.440
Smart.

22:19.980 --> 22:21.200
But even someone like that,

22:21.900 --> 22:23.760
someone who never put a foot wrong…

22:25.820 --> 22:26.660
lost everything

22:28.440 --> 22:29.600
in just one day.

22:35.660 --> 22:36.940
Are you afraid?

22:39.020 --> 22:39.860
Afraid that…

22:40.600 --> 22:42.200
the same thing could happen to you?

22:45.420 --> 22:46.260
No.

22:48.360 --> 22:49.400
When my mom had the accident,

22:49.440 --> 22:50.940
lying on the ward bed,

22:52.460 --> 22:53.760
she told me,

22:53.800 --> 22:54.700
"Jiang Qiaoxi,

22:55.580 --> 22:56.980
you don't know how the world works."

22:58.400 --> 22:59.820
I didn't believe her then.

23:00.780 --> 23:02.280
But six months later,

23:02.320 --> 23:03.780
my cousin had his accident.

23:03.820 --> 23:04.820
That's when I realized…

23:07.500 --> 23:08.500
she was right.

23:08.540 --> 23:09.900
People don't get to choose.

23:10.780 --> 23:11.840
The only real choice…

23:14.700 --> 23:15.820
is whether the world

23:16.680 --> 23:17.980
decides to be on your side.

23:23.420 --> 23:24.900
Jiang Qiaoxi,

23:24.940 --> 23:28.020
don't get stuck in the nihilism crisis.

23:29.760 --> 23:31.600
Come on. People make choices.

23:32.360 --> 23:34.260
We make choices every day.

23:34.300 --> 23:35.220
Look.

23:35.260 --> 23:36.620
Today we chose congee,

23:36.660 --> 23:37.920
so we didn't get

23:37.960 --> 23:39.340
claypot rice.

23:39.380 --> 23:40.700
We picked beer,

23:40.740 --> 23:42.280
so we missed out on lemon tea.

23:42.320 --> 23:43.240
I…

23:44.340 --> 23:45.220
Oh no, I'm so sorry!

23:45.260 --> 23:46.460
I'm so sorry!

23:46.500 --> 23:48.100
Let me bring you a fresh one.

23:48.140 --> 23:48.980
It's fine.

23:49.020 --> 23:49.860
I'm sorry.

23:50.860 --> 23:51.700
Don't worry about it.

23:54.140 --> 23:54.980
Here, use this napkin.

24:00.360 --> 24:01.200
Drink mine if you want.

24:04.740 --> 24:05.580
I've got one.

24:06.720 --> 24:07.580
I've got one.

24:28.040 --> 24:29.420
I should've come to check in sooner.

24:30.260 --> 24:32.700
But the market was rough,

24:32.740 --> 24:34.440
and it took me a while to bounce back.

24:35.360 --> 24:36.740
Before I knew it,

24:36.780 --> 24:38.020
this was the only time I had.

24:38.060 --> 24:39.080
No worries.

24:39.120 --> 24:40.900
If you'd come earlier,

24:40.940 --> 24:44.000
you'd have caught me lying here
pretending to be Sleeping Beauty.

24:45.680 --> 24:46.740
- Cousin. Cousin-in-law.
- Qiaoxi.

24:47.720 --> 24:48.720
- Cousin-in-law.
- Yingtao.

24:48.760 --> 24:49.840
These flowers are for you.

24:50.380 --> 24:51.440
Hi, cousin.

24:51.480 --> 24:52.320
You didn't have to.

24:52.360 --> 24:53.420
- Hey.
- Hi there.

24:54.960 --> 24:55.860
Let me…

25:00.140 --> 25:02.420
You must be Yingtao, right?

25:03.320 --> 25:04.320
That's me.

25:05.000 --> 25:06.280
Hard to believe

25:06.320 --> 25:07.540
it is the first time we meet.

25:08.520 --> 25:10.720
Feels like I've known you forever.

25:11.780 --> 25:13.460
This kid's been talking about you

25:13.500 --> 25:14.880
since he was little.

25:18.200 --> 25:21.020
And Jiang Qiaoxi's always
going on about his cousin.

25:21.900 --> 25:23.540
- Oh yeah?
- Yes.

25:24.160 --> 25:25.140
Yes.

25:26.220 --> 25:28.960
I, um… I brought some snacks for you.

25:29.620 --> 25:30.720
Nothing expensive or fancy.

25:30.760 --> 25:32.700
Just figured hospital food

25:32.740 --> 25:34.880
probably doesn't have much flavor,

25:34.920 --> 25:36.240
so I got a bit of everything.

25:36.280 --> 25:37.920
You're so sweet. That's really thoughtful.

25:38.620 --> 25:39.460
No wonder

25:40.020 --> 25:41.540
Qiaoxi always says nice things about you.

25:42.800 --> 25:44.120
Qiaoxi,

25:44.160 --> 25:46.300
Yingtao lives up to her name.
Sweet as a cherry.

25:48.120 --> 25:49.940
So, this is the little genius

25:49.980 --> 25:51.200
from your family?

25:51.980 --> 25:54.180
Didn't think he'd be this tall.
Or this good-looking.

25:55.720 --> 25:57.820
The Jiangs are just built like that.

25:57.860 --> 25:59.280
Good genes. Can't help it.

25:59.320 --> 26:00.620
My cousin here

26:00.660 --> 26:02.940
now studies
at the University of Hong Kong.

26:02.980 --> 26:05.220
Double major, finance and math.

26:05.260 --> 26:06.420
Top marks across the board.

26:07.340 --> 26:08.700
Hey, isn't that

26:08.740 --> 26:09.940
what you studied too?

26:10.640 --> 26:12.320
If he gets

26:12.360 --> 26:13.460
into the financial sector,

26:13.500 --> 26:15.580
he's bound to make waves.

26:15.620 --> 26:16.460
Big things ahead.

26:17.260 --> 26:18.520
He'll surpass me, no doubt.

26:18.560 --> 26:19.840
I've never worried

26:19.880 --> 26:20.900
about this one.

26:20.940 --> 26:22.320
Hey, cousin,

26:22.360 --> 26:24.160
once you find a good stock,

26:24.200 --> 26:25.560
you better tip me off.

26:25.600 --> 26:27.120
If I can cash out again,

26:27.160 --> 26:29.180
my kids'll be set for life.

26:30.240 --> 26:31.960
- Sure.
- Hey,

26:32.000 --> 26:33.420
- remember that EV stock
- Let me.

26:33.460 --> 26:36.180
you told me to buy?

26:37.140 --> 26:38.980
You kept saying it had serious potential.

26:39.720 --> 26:40.920
So, I convinced my wife

26:40.960 --> 26:42.100
to put all our savings into it.

26:42.900 --> 26:45.020
Two years later, it shot up 14 times.

26:49.700 --> 26:50.540
That's great.

26:51.560 --> 26:52.400
Smart move.

26:52.440 --> 26:54.540
Too bad

26:54.580 --> 26:56.000
he's just lying in bed now.

26:56.040 --> 26:57.560
Totally useless.

26:57.600 --> 26:58.460
Remember

26:58.500 --> 27:00.540
when we worked at that printing factory?

27:00.580 --> 27:01.940
He chewed us out all night

27:01.980 --> 27:03.400
over one typo.

27:03.980 --> 27:05.820
He's not so high and mighty now.

27:05.860 --> 27:07.560
When he heard I was headed to Singapore,

27:07.600 --> 27:08.960
he looked at me

27:09.000 --> 27:10.680
like some sad stray dog.

27:11.280 --> 27:12.120
His wife though?

27:12.160 --> 27:13.340
Still a knockout.

27:14.040 --> 27:14.900
Jiang Qiaoxi.

27:14.940 --> 27:16.720
So pretty, it's ridiculous.

27:16.760 --> 27:18.240
- Jiang Qiaoxi.
- What did you say?

27:19.020 --> 27:20.660
- Let go!
- Don't hit him, Jiang Qiaoxi!

27:20.700 --> 27:21.940
- Let go.
- Get over here.

27:22.820 --> 27:24.840
- Jiang Qiaoxi, calm down!
- Are you crazy?

27:24.880 --> 27:26.100
Qiaoxi!

27:26.140 --> 27:27.500
- Jiang Qiaoxi!
- Qiaoxi!

27:28.840 --> 27:29.680
Let go!

27:31.800 --> 27:32.760
Hey, no violence.

27:41.100 --> 27:42.080
Ruocheng was nice to you.

27:42.120 --> 27:43.800
Have you even visited him once?

27:43.840 --> 27:45.140
How many times did he help you out?

27:46.740 --> 27:48.320
- Hey.
- Don't ever show your face again!

28:05.320 --> 28:07.460
Hello? Hello?

28:07.500 --> 28:08.360
What's going on?

28:08.400 --> 28:09.300
Asshole!

28:20.100 --> 28:20.940
Hey.

28:23.420 --> 28:24.260
Are you okay?

28:25.660 --> 28:26.660
I'm fine.

28:27.580 --> 28:28.420
Are you?

28:29.280 --> 28:30.120
Yeah, I'm okay.

28:30.160 --> 28:31.000
No violence.

28:32.940 --> 28:33.780
Let's go.

28:37.080 --> 28:38.520
I didn't freak you out, did I?

28:39.900 --> 28:40.820
Of course not.

28:41.440 --> 28:43.420
I've always known

28:43.460 --> 28:44.500
what you're like.

28:45.360 --> 28:46.720
What did surprise me

28:46.760 --> 28:48.120
was how your cousin-in-law reacted.

28:48.160 --> 28:50.420
She was like a swordswoman out of…

28:52.480 --> 28:53.460
a wuxia novel.

28:59.900 --> 29:00.740
Yingtao,

29:02.140 --> 29:03.480
do you think

29:03.520 --> 29:05.060
I've changed

29:06.380 --> 29:07.960
after I came to Hong Kong?

29:11.840 --> 29:13.480
Yeah, you have.

29:16.940 --> 29:18.020
What do I do, Yingtao?

29:19.520 --> 29:22.060
Feels like the cracks and bruises on me…

29:24.120 --> 29:25.140
just keep piling up.

29:27.380 --> 29:28.460
Like you didn't have

29:28.500 --> 29:30.520
plenty of cracks and bruises before.

29:32.060 --> 29:33.980
The difference now

29:35.160 --> 29:37.340
is you don't fake it around me anymore.

29:38.120 --> 29:40.380
You don't try to hide it like you used to.

29:42.960 --> 29:44.000
Now,

29:45.340 --> 29:46.860
in front of me,

29:47.480 --> 29:48.840
you are able to close your eyes

29:48.880 --> 29:50.700
and let me know. That's different.

29:52.260 --> 29:53.820
And you don't just charge ahead doing

29:53.860 --> 29:55.160
what you think is good for us

29:55.200 --> 29:56.720
without asking us first.

29:57.760 --> 29:58.980
Back then, you…

30:00.440 --> 30:01.280
Forget it.

30:02.080 --> 30:02.920
All I know

30:05.060 --> 30:06.560
is I like who you are now.

30:19.860 --> 30:20.700
Hi, cousin-in-law.

30:24.120 --> 30:24.960
Okay.

30:26.440 --> 30:28.120
What's up? Are we going upstairs?

30:28.160 --> 30:29.480
No. She said

30:30.000 --> 30:30.900
she's taking us out.

30:31.500 --> 30:32.340
Out?

30:59.260 --> 31:01.400
- Welcome.
- Hi. We booked a private room.

31:01.440 --> 31:02.280
This way, please.

31:07.280 --> 31:08.240
Mind your step.

31:21.300 --> 31:22.160
Don't worry.

31:22.920 --> 31:24.360
Your cousin's got a VIP card here.

31:26.220 --> 31:27.300
There's money on it.

31:31.680 --> 31:33.420
Let's get the three-way
Australian lobster,

31:33.460 --> 31:34.860
steamed crab,

31:36.280 --> 31:37.560
- and premium abalone.
- Got it.

31:37.600 --> 31:39.100
Star grouper.

31:39.140 --> 31:42.340
Asparagus with morels.

31:42.380 --> 31:43.860
And for dessert…

31:43.900 --> 31:46.040
Little Lin, would you like
the bird's nest soup

31:46.080 --> 31:48.200
or the black truffle chocolate cake?

31:48.240 --> 31:50.320
They do both Chinese and Western
desserts really well here.

31:53.200 --> 31:55.300
Honestly, I'm good with either.

31:56.220 --> 31:57.660
- Then we'll have both.
- No problem.

31:58.300 --> 31:59.840
- Thanks. That's it for now.
- Got it.

32:02.840 --> 32:04.760
Can I get a takeaway box too, please?

32:07.160 --> 32:08.360
Little Lin.

32:08.400 --> 32:10.560
I've been so tied up with Ruocheng lately.

32:10.600 --> 32:12.840
I haven't had a proper meal with you.

32:12.880 --> 32:14.320
Sorry about that.

32:14.360 --> 32:15.340
No, it's fine.

32:15.380 --> 32:16.980
Then, let this dinner

32:17.020 --> 32:19.000
be your welcome dinner.

32:19.540 --> 32:20.820
Ruocheng should've joined us,

32:20.860 --> 32:23.540
but since he snuck out before,

32:23.580 --> 32:26.100
the doctors
won't let him leave the hospital.

32:26.140 --> 32:26.980
Sorry about that.

32:27.620 --> 32:29.520
Please, don't be sorry.

32:29.560 --> 32:31.600
If anything, I should
be thanking you and cousin.

32:33.760 --> 32:34.980
Oh, I forgot the wine.

32:36.280 --> 32:38.300
You don't drink much, do you?

32:40.860 --> 32:42.500
Not really.

32:43.220 --> 32:46.580
Maybe a little beer at school parties

32:46.620 --> 32:48.420
or at home.

32:49.760 --> 32:51.240
What about red wine?

32:51.280 --> 32:52.920
Any favorites?

32:53.820 --> 32:55.480
Not much of a wine drinker.

32:57.300 --> 32:59.320
- Fair enough.
- Hey, cousin-in-law.

33:01.420 --> 33:02.800
Fancy wine.

33:02.840 --> 33:03.760
Fancy restaurant.

33:04.580 --> 33:05.760
They can wait.

33:12.780 --> 33:13.620
Qiaoxi,

33:14.780 --> 33:16.200
at the toughest times, like now,

33:17.240 --> 33:19.100
we should drink the best wine,

33:19.140 --> 33:20.220
dine at the best places, right?

33:21.420 --> 33:22.920
Isn't that exactly

33:23.840 --> 33:25.800
when we have to hold
our heads high and live

33:25.840 --> 33:27.600
the decent life to keep
believing in ourselves?

33:32.480 --> 33:33.580
Let's go with what she says.

33:33.620 --> 33:35.300
Let's drink the good wine.

33:36.260 --> 33:37.100
Yes, let's do it.

34:03.520 --> 34:05.200
When I was your age,

34:05.240 --> 34:06.740
I used to read novels all the time.

34:08.659 --> 34:09.500
There was this one,

34:10.760 --> 34:12.100
Wounded City by Yishu.

34:13.880 --> 34:15.080
Back then,

34:15.120 --> 34:16.560
I could never

34:17.219 --> 34:18.840
quite understand the ending.

34:21.540 --> 34:22.380
But today,

34:24.000 --> 34:25.320
I think I finally do.

34:28.060 --> 34:29.880
I read that one.

34:31.020 --> 34:32.380
I know the story.

34:38.440 --> 34:39.360
What was the story?

34:48.440 --> 34:49.280
There is a man

34:51.739 --> 34:53.840
who gets shot in the waist with an arrow.

34:55.159 --> 34:56.159
And…

34:57.180 --> 34:59.320
he just lives with it, never pulls it out.

35:00.560 --> 35:02.400
People ask if it hurts.

35:02.440 --> 35:03.720
He says

35:03.760 --> 35:07.260
it hurts only when he remembers

35:07.300 --> 35:08.680
he has an arrow in the waist.

35:12.700 --> 35:14.720
I brought you both out tonight.

35:15.960 --> 35:17.880
It was meant to lift your spirits.

35:19.760 --> 35:21.000
To remind you

35:21.040 --> 35:23.300
of the good days we once had together.

35:25.120 --> 35:26.320
But sitting here now,

35:26.360 --> 35:28.060
those memories feel more

35:28.100 --> 35:29.720
like that arrow.

35:32.800 --> 35:34.300
Since your cousin's accident,

35:35.500 --> 35:36.720
I've never thought of it as hard.

35:36.760 --> 35:38.200
But Qiaoxi,

35:38.240 --> 35:39.820
you're the one who's sacrificed the most.

35:39.860 --> 35:41.480
You gave up your studies overseas.

35:41.520 --> 35:43.820
Now you're juggling for his medical bills,

35:44.800 --> 35:46.060
with three jobs on your shoulders.

35:46.760 --> 35:48.020
You worked so hard.

35:49.740 --> 35:50.580
Cousin-in-law…

35:52.000 --> 35:53.620
He's my cousin.

35:55.500 --> 35:56.860
Even if you'd told me to leave,

35:58.680 --> 35:59.940
I wouldn't have gone.

36:01.420 --> 36:03.380
If it weren't for everything
with the family,

36:04.880 --> 36:06.900
you and Yingtao wouldn't have spent
so many years apart.

36:09.180 --> 36:10.520
Seeing the two of you now,

36:12.160 --> 36:13.740
my heart aches for what you've lost.

36:13.780 --> 36:15.100
No, cousin-in-law.

36:16.760 --> 36:18.260
Please don't feel that way.

36:19.700 --> 36:21.760
When I met Jiang Qiaoxi,

36:21.800 --> 36:23.700
I knew from the start his cousin

36:23.740 --> 36:24.980
meant everything to him.

36:25.520 --> 36:27.880
If he hadn't stayed,

36:27.920 --> 36:29.720
he wouldn't be the same
Jiang Qiaoxi I know.

36:34.280 --> 36:35.340
I'm sorry.

36:39.780 --> 36:40.840
Here.

36:44.440 --> 36:45.280
Thank you. Both of you.

36:49.840 --> 36:50.760
Jiang Ruocheng.

36:51.960 --> 36:53.880
Ruo, as in something fleeting.

36:53.920 --> 36:54.940
Cheng, as in honesty.

36:56.520 --> 36:57.440
Sorry, sir.

36:57.480 --> 36:59.120
Our restaurant changed hands recently,

36:59.160 --> 37:00.500
and the system's been glitchy.

37:00.540 --> 37:01.920
We won't be able to check your balance

37:01.960 --> 37:02.860
until tomorrow.

37:03.420 --> 37:04.260
We're sorry.

37:05.480 --> 37:06.760
Tomorrow, right?

37:06.800 --> 37:08.020
Yes. We're sorry.

37:09.460 --> 37:10.620
Alright then.

37:10.660 --> 37:11.560
I'll pay in cash.

37:11.600 --> 37:12.940
That'll be 4,512.

37:24.860 --> 37:26.460
Can I use UnionPay?

37:26.500 --> 37:27.960
- UnionPay.
- No, no. I've got my card.

37:30.280 --> 37:31.260
I've got money.

37:32.200 --> 37:34.000
And I've been meaning
to treat her to dinner.

37:36.060 --> 37:37.080
Hands off.

37:47.440 --> 37:48.820
- Thank you.
- Tell…

37:48.860 --> 37:50.140
All settled?

37:50.180 --> 37:51.320
Yep, done.

37:51.360 --> 37:52.760
Thanks for the meal, cousin-in-law.

37:53.700 --> 37:55.360
Food was great, wine was perfect.

37:56.860 --> 37:57.940
I'm totally stuffed.

37:57.980 --> 37:59.520
Why don't we take a walk?

38:01.980 --> 38:02.820
Let me get that.

38:04.140 --> 38:05.200
Hope to see you again.

38:05.240 --> 38:06.220
Thank you.

38:06.260 --> 38:07.460
Hope to see you again.

38:21.640 --> 38:22.480
Qiaoxi,

38:23.060 --> 38:25.260
Yingtao, wait here.
I'm just gonna grab something.

38:25.300 --> 38:26.480
I won't be long.

38:26.520 --> 38:27.720
- Going by yourself?
- Hey…

39:16.980 --> 39:17.820
Mark Six.

39:18.500 --> 39:19.400
Tonight's the draw.

39:20.100 --> 39:20.940
One ticket each.

39:21.600 --> 39:22.640
What made you think

39:22.680 --> 39:23.940
of buying lottery tickets?

39:24.480 --> 39:25.520
Over the past two years,

39:25.560 --> 39:28.080
whenever life felt too hard,

39:29.120 --> 39:30.120
I'd buy one.

39:30.160 --> 39:31.460
It gave me something

39:32.480 --> 39:33.460
to hope for.

39:35.020 --> 39:36.060
Yingtao,

39:36.600 --> 39:37.560
you treated us tonight,

39:38.900 --> 39:40.000
so this is the best

39:40.860 --> 39:42.200
I can do in return. A little luck.

39:42.760 --> 39:43.600
Go ahead. Pick one.

39:44.540 --> 39:45.720
- I get to choose first?
- Yes.

39:46.760 --> 39:47.800
Well…

39:50.060 --> 39:51.540
Then I'll just grab one.

39:52.420 --> 39:53.300
This one.

39:58.680 --> 40:00.200
Wouldn't it be nice

40:00.240 --> 40:01.820
if it actually hit the jackpot?

40:02.480 --> 40:04.280
You have a better shot
at getting hit by lightning

40:04.320 --> 40:05.820
than winning the Mark Six.

40:10.820 --> 40:11.900
Why would you say that?

40:12.600 --> 40:14.260
Way to kill the mood.

40:14.300 --> 40:16.780
Don't rain on our parade, alright?

40:17.660 --> 40:19.320
I think she's right.

40:19.360 --> 40:20.420
It's not just a ticket.

40:21.120 --> 40:21.960
It's hope.

40:26.180 --> 40:28.240
Cousin-in-law, that reminds me.

40:28.280 --> 40:30.040
Jiang Qiaoxi told me the other day

40:30.080 --> 40:31.300
he thinks

40:31.340 --> 40:32.680
people don't get to choose.

40:33.240 --> 40:34.640
The real choice

40:34.680 --> 40:36.300
depends on whether the world

40:36.340 --> 40:37.240
is on your side.

40:37.280 --> 40:38.660
Maybe

40:38.700 --> 40:40.380
there's some truth to that.

40:40.420 --> 40:41.580
But I think

40:42.560 --> 40:44.780
even if the world isn't on our side,

40:45.580 --> 40:46.920
we can still choose.

40:48.000 --> 40:50.640
We can choose to hope.

40:51.500 --> 40:52.500
And that's something

40:53.240 --> 40:54.340
nobody can take from you.

40:55.860 --> 40:57.180
Thank you, cousin-in-law,

40:57.220 --> 40:58.360
for giving me hope.

41:01.720 --> 41:02.920
Thank you, Yingtao.

41:04.900 --> 41:05.880
It's been a long time

41:06.560 --> 41:08.200
since I've heard something like that.

41:11.520 --> 41:12.720
Cousin-in-law,

41:12.760 --> 41:14.020
don't worry.

41:15.920 --> 41:17.360
"Whatever pain you're feeling right now,

41:18.040 --> 41:18.880
it'll pass.

41:19.560 --> 41:21.220
Even the bad things can turn

41:21.260 --> 41:22.640
into something good, eventually."

41:23.460 --> 41:24.960
That's what my dad told me.

41:26.400 --> 41:28.280
And cousin's already

41:28.320 --> 41:29.580
getting better.

41:30.360 --> 41:31.920
Things are only gonna go up from here.

41:37.640 --> 41:38.820
Thank you, Yingtao.

41:46.580 --> 41:48.220
It still blows my mind.

41:49.220 --> 41:50.940
That just one little Mark Six ticket

41:50.980 --> 41:52.580
can carry so much hope.

41:53.120 --> 41:54.100
But if we don't win,

41:54.140 --> 41:55.820
isn't it just a useless piece of paper?

41:55.860 --> 41:58.040
But before 9:30 p.m.,

41:58.080 --> 42:00.400
it's a proof that something good
might happen.

42:02.100 --> 42:04.120
But what if we don't win after 9:30 p.m.?

42:04.160 --> 42:06.080
Isn't that even more disappointing?

42:06.960 --> 42:07.960
Then…

42:08.900 --> 42:10.080
Then we buy another one.

42:10.620 --> 42:11.480
Wait for the next draw.

42:12.000 --> 42:13.680
Keep the hope going for another day.

42:14.400 --> 42:16.800
Don't tell me you're not
even a little curious

42:16.840 --> 42:18.680
if yours might actually win.

42:18.720 --> 42:20.400
Not even the tiniest bit?

42:22.240 --> 42:23.920
Mark Six odds are like

42:23.960 --> 42:25.240
one in ten million.

42:26.020 --> 42:27.640
But the odds of meeting Lin Yingtao?

42:27.680 --> 42:28.920
That's one in a trillion.

42:28.960 --> 42:31.420
So yeah, I already hit the jackpot.

42:34.220 --> 42:35.340
Jiang Qiaoxi.

42:36.160 --> 42:37.380
Since when did you get

42:37.420 --> 42:38.980
this cheesy?

42:39.020 --> 42:39.860
Say that again.

42:39.900 --> 42:41.100
- Good lines only come once.
- Now.

42:41.140 --> 42:42.940
- Nope.
- What time is it now?

42:47.120 --> 42:49.060
- 9:45 p.m.
- Time to check the results.

42:49.100 --> 42:51.040
Let me see. I'll go first.

42:51.760 --> 42:52.600
Here.

42:53.160 --> 42:54.140
You hold it. I'll read it.

42:56.580 --> 42:57.420
Zero-one,

42:57.940 --> 42:58.780
29,

42:59.280 --> 43:00.120
zero-six,

43:00.720 --> 43:01.660
22…

43:01.700 --> 43:02.940
Hold on.

43:03.740 --> 43:05.860
Zero-one, 29, 22.

43:07.700 --> 43:09.160
- Zero-six.
- Zero-six.

43:09.200 --> 43:10.980
Forty-four, 45.

43:11.680 --> 43:12.960
- Forty-five.
- Twenty-seven.

43:13.000 --> 43:14.900
- Thirty-six.
- Twenty-seven. And the last one…

43:14.940 --> 43:15.940
Thirty-six?

43:18.180 --> 43:19.120
Two misses.

43:20.680 --> 43:21.760
Five hits.

43:21.800 --> 43:24.040
Only two misses. That's painful.

43:24.080 --> 43:25.800
Five should still be worth
something, right?

43:26.380 --> 43:27.220
No idea.

43:27.840 --> 43:29.500
As long as there's money, we're good.

43:31.120 --> 43:32.920
How many times are you gonna count?

43:32.960 --> 43:34.640
- Stop it.
- Two, three…

43:34.680 --> 43:36.180
Five main numbers matched.

43:36.760 --> 43:38.660
That's fourth prize.
9,600 Hong Kong dollars.

43:38.700 --> 43:39.900
That's official.

43:40.400 --> 43:41.720
See? I told you.

43:41.760 --> 43:43.560
Even the universe feels sorry for me.

43:43.600 --> 43:45.120
You just didn't believe it.

43:45.820 --> 43:47.740
The universe might feel bad for you,

43:48.460 --> 43:49.560
but if you don't put it away,

43:49.600 --> 43:50.760
even the universe

43:50.800 --> 43:52.200
won't stop you from getting mugged.

43:58.860 --> 44:00.120
Jiang Qiaoxi.

44:00.160 --> 44:01.340
My mom always said,

44:01.380 --> 44:02.420
money like this

44:02.460 --> 44:05.500
from gambling or winning the lottery

44:05.540 --> 44:07.880
isn't earned the right way.

44:07.920 --> 44:09.460
Spend it fast or it brings bad luck.

44:09.500 --> 44:11.060
Let's blow it all here in Hong Kong.

44:12.240 --> 44:13.940
Sure. What are you thinking of buying?

44:16.460 --> 44:17.500
Actually, there is something.

44:18.480 --> 44:19.740
Ray-Ban sunglasses.

44:22.760 --> 44:25.040
For… Yu Qiao?

44:26.660 --> 44:27.500
Who else do you think?

44:28.980 --> 44:30.720
Come on. Let's go. Show me.

46:46.460 --> 46:48.620
Subtitle translation by: Jiaxin Wang
